1
00:00:05,905 --> 00:00:07,374
[thunder rumbling]

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:10,310
[Elmo] "Storm on Sesame Street."

3
00:00:11,778 --> 00:00:13,680
- Let's get another.
- Okay. Almost, Bert.

4
00:00:13,747 --> 00:00:15,415
[both straining]

5
00:00:15,482 --> 00:00:17,784
- Oh, boy, this is heavy.
- [Ernie] Okay. Phew.

6
00:00:19,819 --> 00:00:21,054
[sighs]

7
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:25,792
- Come on in, get your supplies.
- Thanks for the water.

8
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:28,294
- Certainly, Baby Bear.
- You're welcome. Stay safe, Baby Bear.

9
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,397
- [barking]
- Oh, hi.

10
00:00:30,463 --> 00:00:32,332
Elmo's so happy you're here.

11
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:34,968
You know, there's a big storm
coming to Sesame Street,

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:36,836
so we're helping our neighbors.

13
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:41,207
Like Elmo said,
we're handing out extra food and water,

14
00:00:41,274 --> 00:00:44,477
'cause folks will need
to stay inside during the storm.

15
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:45,912
- Yeah.
- Be safe, everyone.

16
00:00:45,979 --> 00:00:48,815
- Uh-huh.
- Together, we'll all get through this.

17
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:52,419
You know, Daddy says
there's gonna be lots of wind

18
00:00:52,485 --> 00:00:55,922
and rain, and thunder and lightning.

19
00:00:56,489 --> 00:00:57,724
[gasping]

20
00:00:58,925 --> 00:01:01,594
Elmo and Tango
don't want this storm to come, Daddy.

21
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:03,463
Yeah, I understand.

22
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:06,566
But unfortunately,
we can't change the weather.

23
00:01:06,633 --> 00:01:08,835
We can prepare for it, though,

24
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:15,208
which is why I need your help,
uh, on a special mission.

25
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:18,611
- Wha… A special mission?
- [Louie] Mm-hm.

26
00:01:18,678 --> 00:01:23,149
- [exciting music playing]
- I need you to find star stickers,

27
00:01:23,216 --> 00:01:26,820
a sock and an ice cream scooper.

28
00:01:26,886 --> 00:01:28,521
- [Tango] Mm?
- Huh?

29
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:31,658
[laughing] I know, they… they seem silly.

30
00:01:31,724 --> 00:01:36,129
But I promise they'll help us
and our friends during the storm.

31
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:41,134
Helping our friends is how
we can show courage during tough times.

32
00:01:41,201 --> 00:01:42,869
Well, you can count on us.

33
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:46,406
Elmo and Tango
can show courage, just like Daddy.

34
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:48,241
I know it. I know you can.

35
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:51,077
Okay, now come on.
Let's start our special mission.

36
00:01:51,144 --> 00:01:52,378
- [giggling]
- [barking]

37
00:01:52,445 --> 00:01:54,447
[news theme music playing]

38
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,619
I'm Sammy Squalls, here on Sesame Street,

39
00:01:59,686 --> 00:02:02,989
where neighbors are helping each other
prepare for the really big storm.

40
00:02:03,056 --> 00:02:05,925
Excuse me, what are your thoughts
on the oncoming storm?

41
00:02:05,992 --> 00:02:07,227
Scram.

42
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:10,663
Yes, absolutely.
We'd all love for this storm to scram.

43
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:13,066
Not the storm, you.

44
00:02:15,101 --> 00:02:17,403
Oh! Any thoughts on the oncoming storm?

45
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,606
Double scram. [laughing]

46
00:02:19,672 --> 00:02:21,274
[in squeaky voice] Okay. There you…

47
00:02:22,041 --> 00:02:24,377
[in normal voice] There you have it.
Back to you.

48
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,415
Okay, I found some more supplies. Here.

49
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:30,650
[Cookie Monster] Oh, good.

50
00:02:30,717 --> 00:02:32,085
[Snuffy] That one's cute, Bird.

51
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,186
They're so cute.

52
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:35,622
Ah, Snuffy, Big Bird. Hi.

53
00:02:35,688 --> 00:02:37,123
- [chuckling] Hi, Elmo.
- Hey, Elmo.

54
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,591
It's really busy in here.

55
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:41,561
Looks like lots of people
are staying at Elmo's for the storm.

56
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:42,729
- Yeah.
- [Abby] Hey, Elmo.

57
00:02:42,795 --> 00:02:43,830
Oh! Coming!

58
00:02:43,897 --> 00:02:44,731
[barking]

59
00:02:45,398 --> 00:02:48,234
Hey, Abby, Rudy, have you seen a…

60
00:02:48,301 --> 00:02:49,302
[shivering]

61
00:02:49,369 --> 00:02:53,339
Abby, oh, I'm so scared.

62
00:02:53,406 --> 00:02:56,943
Everything feels so different outside.

63
00:02:57,577 --> 00:02:59,379
I know, brother. I know.

64
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:03,950
Rudy's right. Sesame Street
does feel different today.

65
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:07,453
Hm. Elmo understands why Rudy's scared.

66
00:03:08,054 --> 00:03:09,656
Can Elmo tell you something?

67
00:03:10,456 --> 00:03:11,791
Elmo's scared too.

68
00:03:12,292 --> 00:03:15,128
But Elmo needs to have courage.

69
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,797
Yeah, Elmo has to help his friend.

70
00:03:18,298 --> 00:03:19,399
Elmo has an idea.

71
00:03:19,465 --> 00:03:22,802
Uh, Rudy, Abby, do you want
to help Elmo and Tango

72
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:24,804
with our special mission?

73
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:27,574
- [exciting music playing]
- [both] Huh? Special mission?

74
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:32,545
Yeah, Elmo's daddy needs us
to find three things: star stickers…

75
00:03:32,612 --> 00:03:33,446
- Uh-huh.
- Oh.

76
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:36,049
…a sock and an ice cream scooper.

77
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:41,354
Elmo doesn't know why, but his daddy
said that they're very important.

78
00:03:41,421 --> 00:03:45,024
Whoa! This must be
a really special mission, then.

79
00:03:45,091 --> 00:03:46,192
[thunder crashing]

80
00:03:46,259 --> 00:03:47,260
It's okay.

81
00:03:47,327 --> 00:03:49,796
Aw! But the storm…

82
00:03:49,862 --> 00:03:51,965
- Is outside.
- Mm-hm.

83
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:54,033
And we're inside.

84
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,869
- So let's start our special mission.
- [exciting music playing]

85
00:03:56,936 --> 00:03:57,971
To the kitchen!

86
00:03:58,037 --> 00:03:59,105
Okay.

87
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:02,075
There you go, Radar.

88
00:04:02,842 --> 00:04:04,277
- Hi.
- Oh!

89
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:05,445
Hi, Snuffy!

90
00:04:05,511 --> 00:04:09,482
[Snuffy] Whoa!
What are you three doing there?

91
00:04:09,549 --> 00:04:12,885
- Well, we're on a special mission.
- Oh?

92
00:04:12,952 --> 00:04:16,889
- Wow. Why so many stuffies?
- Yeah, what's with the stuffies, Snuffy?

93
00:04:16,956 --> 00:04:19,993
Well, storms can be scary, you know.

94
00:04:20,059 --> 00:04:23,830
And you never know
when you might need a hug.

95
00:04:23,896 --> 00:04:27,900
And I like to get mine
from a fuzzy cabbage.

96
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:28,801
[Abby] Aw.

97
00:04:28,868 --> 00:04:32,005
Um, you said something
about a special mission?

98
00:04:32,071 --> 00:04:35,174
Yeah, that's right.
We're looking for star stickers.

99
00:04:35,241 --> 00:04:37,243
- They're very important.
- [exciting music playing]

100
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,912
But we don't know why.
Will you help us look?

101
00:04:39,979 --> 00:04:41,648
- Oh, sure.
- You betcha.

102
00:04:41,714 --> 00:04:42,649
Great. Thank you.

103
00:04:42,715 --> 00:04:44,817
- [Abby] I'm gonna look over here.
- Excuse me.

104
00:04:44,884 --> 00:04:46,152
- [wind gusting]
- Whoa!

105
00:04:46,219 --> 00:04:49,989
Oh, that wind is so loud and scary.

106
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:54,761
It is scary. Elmo's scared too.

107
00:04:54,827 --> 00:04:58,831
But Elmo needs to have courage
and help his friends.

108
00:04:58,898 --> 00:05:02,168
Maybe with a fuzzy hug.

109
00:05:02,235 --> 00:05:08,174
See? That wasn't the wind, Rudy.
That was just dragon roaring for a hug.

110
00:05:08,241 --> 00:05:12,211
Oh! A dragon! I like that.

111
00:05:12,712 --> 00:05:15,348
Oh! Look! There's the stickers!

112
00:05:15,415 --> 00:05:16,449
Yeah!

113
00:05:16,516 --> 00:05:18,418
[all exclaiming happily]

114
00:05:18,484 --> 00:05:22,221
All right, come on. There's more
to find on our special mission.

115
00:05:22,288 --> 00:05:26,559
Yeah, that's right. We have to find
a sock and an ice cream scooper.

116
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:32,231
And Elmo knows where to look next:
Bert and Ernie's apartment. Yay!

117
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:35,301
Oh! Ernie, Bert, we need help with our…

118
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:36,235
special…

119
00:05:36,302 --> 00:05:37,303
mission.

120
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:39,205
Yeah, that's right.

121
00:05:39,272 --> 00:05:43,209
Bert, it's a really important mission,
okay?

122
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:45,712
[Bert] Rudy, we're over here.

123
00:05:45,778 --> 00:05:48,915
- The animals stole our laundry.
- Give me that.

124
00:05:48,981 --> 00:05:51,417
- Why do you have all these animals?
- Stop, you!

125
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:54,587
Well, we're taking care of them
during the storm. See?

126
00:05:54,654 --> 00:05:58,925
We're giving them food and water
and a safe place to stay.

127
00:05:58,991 --> 00:06:01,694
And they're giving us nothing but trouble.

128
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:02,929
Come back here!

129
00:06:02,995 --> 00:06:07,166
Hey, look, look, look! A sock!
Oh! Could we have that sock, Ernie?

130
00:06:07,233 --> 00:06:09,001
[grunting] Oh, sure you can.

131
00:06:09,068 --> 00:06:11,738
What? Oh! If you can catch it.

132
00:06:11,804 --> 00:06:12,905
[groaning]

133
00:06:12,972 --> 00:06:14,707
- [thunder rumbling]
- [all gasping]

134
00:06:15,274 --> 00:06:18,244
That thunder is so loud and scary.

135
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:21,347
- [gentle music playing]
- The storm is getting scary.

136
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:24,183
But Elmo needs to have courage
for his friends.

137
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:27,787
Hey, Rudy, look.
The sound of the thunder is scary.

138
00:06:27,854 --> 00:06:29,856
- Yeah.
- But this isn't.

139
00:06:29,922 --> 00:06:31,924
[rattling]

140
00:06:31,991 --> 00:06:32,859
[giggling]

141
00:06:33,459 --> 00:06:35,461
Grab an instrument, everybody.

142
00:06:37,864 --> 00:06:40,233
- Huh? Whoa.
- [gentle tune playing]

143
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:51,377
[Abby] Aw.

144
00:06:51,444 --> 00:06:55,448
Well, look at that.
Your idea helped the animals feel better.

145
00:06:55,515 --> 00:06:58,785
- You helped me feel better too, Elmo.
- [exciting music playing]

146
00:06:58,851 --> 00:07:00,620
- Thank you.
- Aw, you're welcome.

147
00:07:00,686 --> 00:07:01,788
[Abby giggling]

148
00:07:02,889 --> 00:07:03,856
And…

149
00:07:04,957 --> 00:07:06,826
we got the sock!

150
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:09,128
[all] Yay!

151
00:07:09,195 --> 00:07:11,631
Now, let's go back upstairs
to Elmo's apartment.

152
00:07:11,697 --> 00:07:13,966
Yeah, we still need to get
the ice cream scooper.

153
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:15,968
- Oh, yeah, that's right.
- Bye.

154
00:07:16,035 --> 00:07:17,203
Bye now!

155
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:20,273
So, uh, you wanna play checkers, Bert?

156
00:07:20,339 --> 00:07:22,942
[Bert] Ernie, I'm over here.

157
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:24,677
[snickering]

158
00:07:25,244 --> 00:07:26,345
[snickering]

159
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:31,918
Phew! It is really raining out there.
Thanks so much for inviting me in.

160
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:33,619
Oh, happy to have you.

161
00:07:33,686 --> 00:07:37,356
Oh, Sammy Squalls! In my apartment! Oh!

162
00:07:37,423 --> 00:07:41,327
Tonight's top story: your place is lovely!

163
00:07:41,394 --> 00:07:43,396
- Aw.
- Oh! Thank you so much. Oh!

164
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:47,366
And this just in: Yuck. [groaning]

165
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:49,268
Pleasure as always, Oscar.

166
00:07:49,335 --> 00:07:50,970
Is there a good place for my go bag?

167
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,772
- You put it down right there.
- Okay.

168
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:56,776
Good idea having a bag packed to take
with you in case the storm gets worse

169
00:07:56,843 --> 00:07:58,077
and you need to go quickly.

170
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:01,881
Oh, yes. Our go bag
has all our most important stuff.

171
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:04,083
Phones, medicine, food, water.

172
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:08,421
Oh, yeah.
That's kind of like my scram bag.

173
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:11,290
It has all my most important stuff:

174
00:08:11,357 --> 00:08:14,494
- smelly trash.
- [Mae] Ugh!

175
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:15,495
Oh, wow. Okay.

176
00:08:15,561 --> 00:08:19,432
Ms. Sammy Squalls, let's find you
a less stinky place to rest, huh?

177
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,601
- [Cookie Monster] Way ahead of you.
- Oh!

178
00:08:23,069 --> 00:08:26,038
- What are you doing?
- Oh, we inflating this bed.

179
00:08:26,105 --> 00:08:28,241
Yeah, just unfurl it here.

180
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:30,610
And me going to turn it on.

181
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:32,111
Oh, good. This is working.

182
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:34,981
- Oh, yeah.
- Oh, it's working a little too well.

183
00:08:35,047 --> 00:08:36,916
Okay, you can turn it off now.

184
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:40,052
- It's a little big.
- Breaking news: I'm getting squished.

185
00:08:40,119 --> 00:08:43,256
Oh, yeah. Nice and comfy. Yeah.

186
00:08:43,322 --> 00:08:44,290
Help me.

187
00:08:45,091 --> 00:08:47,693
Elmo, how'd your special mission go?

188
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:50,363
Well, we got the star stickers
and the sock.

189
00:08:50,429 --> 00:08:52,798
- Yeah.
- But no ice cream scooper yet.

190
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:54,901
- Then you better keep lookin'.
- Yeah.

191
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:59,105
You know, speaking of looking,
has anybody seen my microphone?

192
00:08:59,171 --> 00:09:00,806
It got lost when I got squished.

193
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:03,309
It might have fallen in my scram bag here.

194
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:04,544
- Let me check.
- Yeah!

195
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:09,682
Let's see.
We got an old hairbrush, an old tuba,

196
00:09:09,749 --> 00:09:13,286
a dirty boot, an ice cream scooper.

197
00:09:13,352 --> 00:09:15,621
Oh, an even dirtier boot.

198
00:09:15,688 --> 00:09:17,690
Wait a minute, Oscar. We need that.

199
00:09:17,757 --> 00:09:19,325
What, the dirtier boot?

200
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:22,061
I knew you couldn't be all bad, Elmo.
Sure. Here.

201
00:09:22,128 --> 00:09:23,796
No, no, no, the ice cream scoop.

202
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:26,399
Hey! We found all three items.

203
00:09:26,465 --> 00:09:28,834
- Yes! We did it!
- Oh! All right!

204
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:30,036
[thunder rumbling]

205
00:09:30,102 --> 00:09:31,771
- Uh-oh.
- Oh, no.

206
00:09:31,837 --> 00:09:34,440
Oh, looks like the power's out.

207
00:09:34,507 --> 00:09:35,374
Yeah.

208
00:09:35,975 --> 00:09:37,577
Everyone all right?

209
00:09:38,344 --> 00:09:39,445
Elmo?

210
00:09:40,646 --> 00:09:42,348
Where are you, son?

211
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:44,417
[gentle music playing]

212
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:49,322
Elmo's scared of the big storm, Daddy.

213
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:54,360
Elmo tried to have courage,
but the storm is too scary.

214
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:55,995
[thunder rumbling]

215
00:09:57,229 --> 00:09:58,831
Oh, here. Come on.

216
00:09:58,898 --> 00:10:00,533
Take my hand, son.

217
00:10:02,802 --> 00:10:07,273
There we go. Now, squeeze it three times.

218
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:09,308
- Count with me?
- Okay.

219
00:10:09,375 --> 00:10:13,779
[both] One. Two. Three.

220
00:10:14,246 --> 00:10:15,314
[both sigh]

221
00:10:15,414 --> 00:10:16,582
You know,

222
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,051
the storm scares me too.

223
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:22,054
Really? Daddy gets scared?

224
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:24,490
But Daddy has so much courage.

225
00:10:24,557 --> 00:10:27,927
I do. And so do you.

226
00:10:27,994 --> 00:10:32,999
Courage is feeling scared
and still helping others.

227
00:10:33,566 --> 00:10:35,067
And you've done that.

228
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:38,104
You did a great job helping Rudy.

229
00:10:38,604 --> 00:10:41,140
You got a lot of courage, son.

230
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,275
I'm proud of you.

231
00:10:43,342 --> 00:10:45,911
Oh. Thank you, Daddy.

232
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:47,279
[both laughing]

233
00:10:49,048 --> 00:10:52,518
Oh, here, give me those stickers
you found on your special mission.

234
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:53,919
- Okay. Here you go.
- All right.

235
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:58,591
Everybody, uh, put these stickers
on your flashlights

236
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:01,193
just like this.

237
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,529
Now, check this out.

238
00:11:03,596 --> 00:11:04,463
[Elmo] Oh…

239
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,699
- [Louie laughing]
- [all exclaiming]

240
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:08,067
[Louie] Huh?

241
00:11:09,435 --> 00:11:12,004
It's good to be together.

242
00:11:12,071 --> 00:11:14,807
Together, we can get through anything.

243
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:17,076
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

244
00:11:17,143 --> 00:11:19,211
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

245
00:11:19,278 --> 00:11:22,648
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪</i>

246
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:27,453
<i>♪ Oh, the storm may be outside ♪</i>

247
00:11:28,254 --> 00:11:32,558
<i>♪ But we're right here and by your side ♪</i>

248
00:11:32,625 --> 00:11:36,328
<i>♪ If you're scared or have a fright ♪</i>

249
00:11:37,096 --> 00:11:40,800
<i>♪ We'll hold you close and tight ♪</i>

250
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:44,503
<i>♪ Let the thunder crack and boom ♪</i>

251
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,505
[thunder rumbling]

252
00:11:46,572 --> 00:11:50,509
<i>♪ We're together inside this room ♪</i>

253
00:11:50,576 --> 00:11:52,778
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

254
00:11:52,845 --> 00:11:54,847
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

255
00:11:54,914 --> 00:11:58,350
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪</i>

256
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:03,589
<i>♪ When we're together</i>
<i>We'll get through any weather ♪</i>

257
00:12:03,656 --> 00:12:07,593
<i>♪ I'm here, I'm here for you ♪</i>

258
00:12:08,094 --> 00:12:11,797
<i>♪ Let's laugh and have some fun ♪</i>

259
00:12:11,864 --> 00:12:12,798
[Grover giggling]

260
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:16,969
<i>♪ Wait until the storm is done ♪</i>

261
00:12:17,036 --> 00:12:21,307
<i>♪ Our friends are all around ♪</i>

262
00:12:21,807 --> 00:12:26,512
<i>♪ This is where the love is found ♪</i>

263
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,447
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

264
00:12:28,514 --> 00:12:30,616
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪</i>

265
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:33,786
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪</i>

266
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:39,291
<i>♪ Elmo believes, believes in you ♪</i>

267
00:12:39,358 --> 00:12:43,462
<i>♪ With courage we'll make it through ♪</i>

268
00:12:44,029 --> 00:12:48,200
<i>♪ When we're together</i>
<i>We'll get through any weather ♪</i>

269
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:52,104
<i>♪ Together me and you ♪</i>

270
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:56,342
<i>♪ Together me and you ♪</i>

271
00:12:56,408 --> 00:12:57,710
[Tango howling]

272
00:12:58,711 --> 00:12:59,578
[giggles]

273
00:13:00,246 --> 00:13:01,380
Wait a minute.

274
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:04,383
Daddy, what did we need
the ice cream scoop for?

275
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,652
Oh… [laughs] Of course!

276
00:13:06,719 --> 00:13:09,355
Well, for the most important thing of all.

277
00:13:09,421 --> 00:13:10,756
Ice cream, everyone!

278
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:12,691
- [Ernie] Oh yeah!
- [Big Bird] Wow! Ice cream!

279
00:13:12,758 --> 00:13:15,261
- Oh, Elmo loves ice cream.
- Yeah.

280
00:13:15,327 --> 00:13:17,429
And Elmo really loves his friends.

281
00:13:17,496 --> 00:13:20,166
We can weather anything together.

282
00:13:21,867 --> 00:13:23,536
[Mae] All right, Alan, get scoopin'.

283
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:27,506
- [thunder cracks]
- [wind whistling]

284
00:13:32,278 --> 00:13:35,080
[Abby] Oh, no, Elmo, look at our street.

285
00:13:35,147 --> 00:13:36,549
The sign!

286
00:13:37,049 --> 00:13:39,251
Oh. There you are.

287
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:41,921
It's good to see you on Sesame Street,

288
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:46,559
but Sesame Street
doesn't really look like Sesame Street.

289
00:13:46,625 --> 00:13:51,096
Yeah. Everything's different
after the big storm.

290
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:53,165
[news theme music playing]

291
00:13:55,801 --> 00:13:58,904
Reporter Sammy Squalls here,
live on Sesame Street.

292
00:13:58,971 --> 00:14:02,541
And after the storm,
there is a lot to fix here.

293
00:14:02,608 --> 00:14:05,010
Fallen trees, flooded apartments.

294
00:14:05,077 --> 00:14:07,880
It just doesn't look like the neighborhood
we all know and love.

295
00:14:07,947 --> 00:14:09,748
And this reporter has to wonder,

296
00:14:09,815 --> 00:14:12,585
when will Sesame Street
feel like home again?

297
00:14:12,651 --> 00:14:14,787
- [groans] You're back?
- Yuck.

298
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:16,889
Okay, um, Oscar, what do you think?

299
00:14:16,956 --> 00:14:20,292
When will Sesame Street feel
like home again? And don't say scram.

300
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:24,063
[groans] Well, if I can't say scram,
he will.

301
00:14:24,129 --> 00:14:26,098
Scram!

302
00:14:26,165 --> 00:14:27,233
[both laughing]

303
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:33,105
Um… [clears throat] Let's ask someone
who's a little less grouchy.

304
00:14:35,507 --> 00:14:38,878
Oh. It doesn't feel like home.

305
00:14:38,944 --> 00:14:40,779
And I really want to help.

306
00:14:40,846 --> 00:14:44,083
But the problem is so big. What can we do?

307
00:14:44,149 --> 00:14:46,652
- [heroic music plays]
- Oh!

308
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:51,323
What if Elmo and Abby were superheroes?

309
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,826
- Huh?
- Then we could totally help Sesame Street!

310
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:55,294
Yeah! Let's do it!

311
00:14:56,128 --> 00:14:59,164
But wait. We still need one thing.

312
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:02,534
Aha!

313
00:15:03,135 --> 00:15:05,771
Elmo, are those your pillow cases?

314
00:15:05,838 --> 00:15:09,575
Not anymore. They're our superhero capes.

315
00:15:09,642 --> 00:15:11,243
- Huh?
- Elmo will be…

316
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:16,815
- [heroic music playing]
- Super Elmo with super strength!

317
00:15:18,350 --> 00:15:23,122
And I am Super Abby with super speed!

318
00:15:24,623 --> 00:15:29,094
And she's Super Tango
with super cute ears.

319
00:15:29,161 --> 00:15:30,129
[panting]

320
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:34,166
Dun-da-da-daa!

321
00:15:34,233 --> 00:15:37,036
C'mon, Super Abby and Super Tango!

322
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:41,140
Let's make Sesame Street
feel like home again!

323
00:15:41,206 --> 00:15:42,308
Yes!

324
00:15:42,808 --> 00:15:44,643
- Cookie Monster.
- Oh, yeah, hi.

325
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:47,579
- Hi. Can you help me answer a question?
- Oh, yeah, sure.

326
00:15:47,646 --> 00:15:49,448
Awesome. When do you think

327
00:15:49,515 --> 00:15:51,684
that Sesame Street
will start to feel like home again?

328
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:54,987
Oh, okay. Well, me think that--

329
00:15:55,054 --> 00:15:56,655
- Da-da-da…
- Uh…

330
00:15:56,722 --> 00:15:58,757
- Yes? Oh, okay.
- Excuse me second.

331
00:15:58,824 --> 00:16:00,993
Grover, what you doing?

332
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:04,063
I am building a rocket ship
to go to the moon.

333
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:08,934
They do not have any storms there.
So, moon, here I come. [laughs]

334
00:16:09,001 --> 00:16:12,671
Grover, are you sure you can go
to the moon in this thing?

335
00:16:12,738 --> 00:16:17,109
Of course I am sure.
Well, my rocket ship is ready.

336
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:19,878
That is supposed to do that.

337
00:16:19,945 --> 00:16:22,982
Before you go, Grover,
can I interview you about the storm?

338
00:16:23,048 --> 00:16:26,685
Nope. Because there will be
no storms where I am going.

339
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:28,988
See you soon, moon.

340
00:16:29,054 --> 00:16:34,026
In three, two, one, blast off!

341
00:16:34,093 --> 00:16:35,194
[rattling]

342
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,595
Whoa.

343
00:16:37,262 --> 00:16:38,664
[clattering]

344
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:41,734
Am I on the moon?

345
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,236
- Uh, no.
- Ugh.

346
00:16:44,303 --> 00:16:46,305
Dun-da-da-da!

347
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:49,108
Super Abby and Super Tango,

348
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:52,578
we need to find a way
to help Sesame Street.

349
00:16:52,644 --> 00:16:56,582
Yes, we're going to make it feel
like home again!

350
00:16:56,648 --> 00:16:57,750
[groans]

351
00:16:57,816 --> 00:17:01,987
How's a Grouch supposed to be grouchy
when he has to deal with all this?

352
00:17:02,054 --> 00:17:04,857
Oh, just like that. Heh, heh, heh.

353
00:17:04,923 --> 00:17:07,292
Look! Our sign fell down.

354
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:10,462
Maybe we can use
our superpowers to fix it.

355
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:11,930
Oh! Yeah!

356
00:17:11,997 --> 00:17:15,901
Elmo can use his super strength!

357
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:17,970
[heroic music playing]

358
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:21,373
[straining]

359
00:17:23,475 --> 00:17:24,610
Try this way.

360
00:17:24,676 --> 00:17:26,045
[straining]

361
00:17:26,645 --> 00:17:28,113
[clattering]

362
00:17:28,947 --> 00:17:30,682
[groaning]

363
00:17:30,749 --> 00:17:32,951
That wasn't very super.

364
00:17:33,018 --> 00:17:36,889
[sighs] Elmo doesn't know
if he can help with a job this big.

365
00:17:36,955 --> 00:17:39,425
[Slimey moaning sadly]

366
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:43,796
What's going on, Slimey?

367
00:17:43,862 --> 00:17:46,598
Aw, it's his clothes.

368
00:17:46,665 --> 00:17:49,902
When the storm hit,
they got all scattered in the wind.

369
00:17:49,968 --> 00:17:50,803
[Abby] Aw.

370
00:17:50,869 --> 00:17:53,338
Oh, yeah.

371
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:55,507
Oh, hey!

372
00:17:56,008 --> 00:17:58,911
Hey, Elmo found your sweater.

373
00:17:58,977 --> 00:18:01,480
Look at this! I found your little hat.

374
00:18:01,547 --> 00:18:03,282
And Tango found your shirt.

375
00:18:03,348 --> 00:18:04,850
Itty-bitty pajamas!

376
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,518
A tiny sneaker.

377
00:18:07,553 --> 00:18:10,823
And eensy-weensy polka-dotty pants!

378
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:12,524
Go!

379
00:18:13,025 --> 00:18:15,294
Thank you!

380
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,463
You're welcome, Slimey.

381
00:18:17,529 --> 00:18:20,099
[sighs] But Elmo just helped a little.

382
00:18:20,165 --> 00:18:25,904
Oh. Super Elmo and Super Abby still need
to find a big way to help Sesame Street.

383
00:18:25,971 --> 00:18:29,508
Yeah. And make it feel like home again.

384
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:31,710
Dun-da-da-da!

385
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:36,381
And so, we're working as fast as we can
to get the lights on in your apartment.

386
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:38,016
Aw, thanks, Calvin.

387
00:18:38,083 --> 00:18:41,353
Yeah. We really appreciate
all you utility workers are doing

388
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,155
to keep us safe after the storm.

389
00:18:43,222 --> 00:18:44,590
- Yeah.
- Well, that's our job.

390
00:18:44,656 --> 00:18:45,757
Yeah. Mm.

391
00:18:46,258 --> 00:18:47,793
Bert? Ernie?

392
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:48,827
What happened?

393
00:18:48,894 --> 00:18:52,898
Oh, all that rain from the storm
flooded our apartment.

394
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:55,367
Almost everything we own is ruined.

395
00:18:55,434 --> 00:18:58,003
Yeah, including all my joke books.

396
00:18:58,070 --> 00:18:59,538
I mean, look at this.

397
00:18:59,605 --> 00:19:01,373
Hey, Bert. Knock, knock.

398
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,575
- Who's there?
- I don't know!

399
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:04,576
Aw.

400
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:08,313
Ernie and Bert, Elmo's so sorry.

401
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:12,017
But the good news is we can help.

402
00:19:12,084 --> 00:19:15,287
- Because we're superheroes.
- [heroic music playing]

403
00:19:15,354 --> 00:19:18,390
Yeah. And I can use my super speed.

404
00:19:18,457 --> 00:19:20,859
I will run, run, run
around your apartment,

405
00:19:20,926 --> 00:19:26,198
waving my arms really fast in the air
until it blows your stuff nice and dry!

406
00:19:26,265 --> 00:19:29,201
Woo-hoo! Swish, swish,
swish, swish, swish, swish!

407
00:19:29,268 --> 00:19:33,872
Dry, dry, dry, dry.
Woo-hoo. Wha-hoo-hoo-ha!

408
00:19:33,939 --> 00:19:36,542
So how's it look? Are they dry?

409
00:19:36,608 --> 00:19:37,609
Um…

410
00:19:37,709 --> 00:19:40,979
- No. Still pretty wet.
- I'll try one more time.

411
00:19:41,046 --> 00:19:44,583
Swish, swish, swish, whoo! [laughing]

412
00:19:44,650 --> 00:19:45,817
[clattering]

413
00:19:46,385 --> 00:19:47,653
[groans]

414
00:19:47,719 --> 00:19:49,788
That wasn't so super.

415
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:52,157
Aw, thanks for trying, Abby.

416
00:19:52,224 --> 00:19:56,228
But it'll be okay.
We have help drying out our place.

417
00:19:56,295 --> 00:20:01,033
Yeah, but even once it's dry, we still
lost a lot of stuff we'll never get back.

418
00:20:01,099 --> 00:20:02,067
I'm just…

419
00:20:02,568 --> 00:20:04,570
I'm just so sad.

420
00:20:04,636 --> 00:20:07,372
Oh, I'm sorry, Ernie.

421
00:20:07,439 --> 00:20:11,176
I'd be sad too
if my favorite things got ruined.

422
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:13,745
I just wish I had my jokes back.

423
00:20:13,812 --> 00:20:15,781
They always make me feel better.

424
00:20:15,847 --> 00:20:20,185
[gasps] Well, I could tell you
my favorite joke.

425
00:20:20,752 --> 00:20:22,821
- Yeah?
- Yeah. Yeah. Okay…

426
00:20:23,322 --> 00:20:28,527
Um, if you have 10 apples in one hand
and 12 oranges in the other,

427
00:20:28,594 --> 00:20:30,229
what have you got?

428
00:20:30,295 --> 00:20:31,363
Uh, what?

429
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:32,931
Big hands.

430
00:20:32,998 --> 00:20:34,900
[all laughing]

431
00:20:34,967 --> 00:20:37,469
- Bert! I love it! Oh, Abby!
- Yes!

432
00:20:37,536 --> 00:20:41,039
I'm gonna remember that
and write it down in my new joke book.

433
00:20:41,106 --> 00:20:43,775
Oh, thank you, Abby.

434
00:20:43,842 --> 00:20:48,080
Aw, you're welcome, Ernie.
But I just helped a little.

435
00:20:48,146 --> 00:20:52,818
Yeah, we still have to keep looking
for the one big thing we can do

436
00:20:52,884 --> 00:20:55,787
to help Sesame Street
feel like home again.

437
00:20:55,854 --> 00:21:00,959
Maybe there's a way for Super Elmo
and Super Abby to help at Hooper's.

438
00:21:01,026 --> 00:21:02,027
Come on.

439
00:21:03,061 --> 00:21:05,063
Dun-da-da…

440
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:08,066
[all] Aw. Oh, no!

441
00:21:09,534 --> 00:21:11,303
Super Abby?

442
00:21:11,370 --> 00:21:14,973
Elmo's not sure
we can fix a problem this big.

443
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,342
We're not real superheroes.

444
00:21:17,409 --> 00:21:20,712
We don't have superpowers,
so we can't help.

445
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:21,747
[sighs]

446
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:26,885
We tried all day
to make Sesame Street feel like home.

447
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:29,187
Maybe it never will.

448
00:21:29,254 --> 00:21:31,823
- [objects clattering]
- Huh? What?

449
00:21:31,890 --> 00:21:34,526
- Grover, you are making me very nervous.
- Be careful.

450
00:21:34,593 --> 00:21:36,995
Grover? What is Grover doing?

451
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:38,363
Going to the moon, Elmo.

452
00:21:38,430 --> 00:21:42,167
And yes, before you ask,
of course I will send you a postcard.

453
00:21:42,234 --> 00:21:43,302
[Elmo giggling]

454
00:21:43,368 --> 00:21:46,305
Uh, Grover, how are you going
to go to the moon?

455
00:21:46,371 --> 00:21:48,774
Your boosters are boots.

456
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:53,278
I am certainly not staying here.
On the moon, there are no storms.

457
00:21:53,345 --> 00:21:55,580
You want to go where there are no storms?

458
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,182
Yes, exactly.

459
00:21:57,249 --> 00:22:01,486
On Sesame Street,
another storm could come.

460
00:22:01,553 --> 00:22:05,724
And the last time, I was so scared.

461
00:22:06,224 --> 00:22:08,360
I do not want to feel that way again.

462
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:10,295
Yeah, Grover's right.

463
00:22:10,362 --> 00:22:12,964
The storm was really scary.

464
00:22:13,031 --> 00:22:15,133
Elmo was scared too.

465
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,602
But we're here for you, Grover.

466
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:20,205
- Yeah, all your friends are.
- Yeah.

467
00:22:20,272 --> 00:22:21,540
Really?

468
00:22:21,606 --> 00:22:24,209
Yes. Really.

469
00:22:24,276 --> 00:22:27,179
Um, can Elmo give Grover a hug?

470
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:29,381
I would like that.

471
00:22:32,451 --> 00:22:33,285
[clattering]

472
00:22:33,352 --> 00:22:36,254
- Whoa!
- Oh, dear.

473
00:22:36,321 --> 00:22:40,225
Yeah. Probably for the best
I did not fly anywhere in that.

474
00:22:40,792 --> 00:22:44,029
But thank you. That hug helped.

475
00:22:44,096 --> 00:22:45,364
Aw.

476
00:22:45,430 --> 00:22:47,165
We just helped a little.

477
00:22:47,232 --> 00:22:49,935
No matter what Elmo and Abby tried,

478
00:22:50,001 --> 00:22:53,171
we couldn't find one big way
to help Sesame Street.

479
00:22:53,238 --> 00:22:56,007
But I did not need something big.

480
00:22:56,074 --> 00:22:59,177
Just one little hug helped me feel better.

481
00:22:59,244 --> 00:23:04,216
Yeah, and that joke you told me
might have seemed like one little thing.

482
00:23:04,282 --> 00:23:06,351
But it really, really helped us.

483
00:23:06,418 --> 00:23:07,252
Mm-hm.

484
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:10,088
Finding Slimey's clothes
helped him feel better too.

485
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:13,325
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- It might seem little, but…

486
00:23:13,825 --> 00:23:15,560
Tha-a-a-a…

487
00:23:15,627 --> 00:23:16,628
Ugh.

488
00:23:16,695 --> 00:23:18,597
Tha-a-a-a…

489
00:23:19,197 --> 00:23:20,232
Thank you.

490
00:23:20,298 --> 00:23:23,435
Uh, yeah, what he said.

491
00:23:23,502 --> 00:23:27,706
When a neighborhood like ours
goes through something really hard…

492
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:32,344
it's not gonna get fixed by a superhero
swooping in and saving the day.

493
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:34,479
It'll be us helping each other.

494
00:23:34,546 --> 00:23:37,382
That's right, Chris. And you know what?

495
00:23:37,449 --> 00:23:41,086
You do not have
to have superpowers to help.

496
00:23:41,153 --> 00:23:46,057
Now see? You already did
help your friends just by being you.

497
00:23:46,124 --> 00:23:49,461
- Yeah.
- But what we did was so little.

498
00:23:49,961 --> 00:23:52,364
